\date{2026-07-10}
\title{Lilypond snippets in Forester}

\p{I built a simple preprocessor that can extract arbitrary blocks from Forester source and run them through an external tool, replacing the block with an image. I then put the whole thing together into a [Shake](https://hackage.haskell.org/package/shake) [build system for my forest](https://github.com/byorgey/forest/blob/main/Shake.hs).  Now I can include musical snippets, like this:}

\lilypond{\verb<<<|
  \relative
  { \time 4/4 \key c \major
    c'4 c g' g a a g2
  }
<<<}

\p{I've been slowly adding musical snippets to identify the first few bars of pieces in my [piano repertoire](00H7).  For example, check out [[00HA]].}

\p{Next I'll extend the preprocessor to work with [diagrams](https://diagrams.github.io/) as well.}
